# Touch fling: make kinetic scrolling behave like a phone.
# Merged from 5 patches: webkit-kinetic-decel-friction-env,
# webkit-kinetic-jank-resilient-end, webkit-touch-gesture-began-phase,
# webkit-wheel-coalesce-phase-split, webkit-kinetic-fling-velocity-fixes.
# Device-verified together on franceinfo.fr / YouTube (build 589-590).
#
# ROOT CAUSE of dead flings: the WPE touch recogniser never emitted
# Phase::Began, so isGestureStart() was never true and the scrolling tree never
# latched a flick to a node — every wheel event hit-tested independently, so on
# a page with nested scrollers the motion events built one scroll controller's
# velocity history while the Ended event that arms the fling landed on a
# different, empty one. The fling then saw a single sample, velocity 0, and the
# page stopped dead. Emitting Began on the first scroll event of each gesture
# binds the whole gesture to one node: dead flings 8/9 -> ~1/9.
#
# The other four:
#  - canCoalesce()'s phase guard is Cocoa-only upstream, so on a busy page the
#    coalescer could merge a whole flick's motion events and its zero-delta
#    Ended event into ONE Phase::Ended event — the same single-sample dead fling
#    by a second route (WEBKIT_WHEEL_COALESCE_PHASE_SPLIT=0 restores stock).
#  - deceleration friction is desktop tuning at 4; WEBKIT_KINETIC_DECEL_FRICTION
#    lowers it for the longer, smoother glide phone flicking expects (the
#    browser sets the device default in apps/browser/main.cpp).
#  - a catch-up tick after a main-thread stall has near-zero dt, so the per-tick
#    "moved < 1px" stop-test fired at high velocity and killed the fling; only
#    trust that test over a real frame interval.
#  - velocity-estimate corrections: measure across motion samples only
#    (WEBKIT_KINETIC_END_EVENT_FIX), drop the 1.09-1.12x N/(N-1) inflation
#    (WEBKIT_KINETIC_VELOCITY_BIAS_FIX), and bound stacked-flick accumulation so
#    feed-scrolling stops running away (WEBKIT_KINETIC_VELOCITY_ACCUM_MAX /
#    WEBKIT_KINETIC_MAX_VELOCITY).
#
# Only heavy real sites reproduce the dead-fling case; a synthetic page will not.
#
# ---
